      "side": 1,
      "message": "It is not common (not as common as defaulting to false for obvious reasons) but it is done. Given that we already have dozens of usages of java_sdk_library that rely on it being true we have no choice about the default. We could rename it to not_shared_library, flip the default and flip the checks but \"Not_\" or even \"No_\" is even less common than BoolDefault(..., true).",
